# Cloudflare Pages _headers — cache control + security headers + CSP.
#
# v9.2 — production-grade CSP from architecture AAR `2026-07-31-portfolio-v9-2-backend-architecture.md` §14.
# The architecture mandates a nonce-based CSP, but Cloudflare Pages `_headers` is
# STATIC — it cannot mint a per-request nonce. The two-layer model:
#
# 1. Static `_headers` (this file) sets a strict-by-default CSP with `'unsafe-inline'`
#    for `script-src`, `style-src`, and `connect-src` because Astro emits ~202 inline
#    `<script type="module">` hydration blocks + 90 inline `<script>` blocks + 145
#    inline `<style>` blocks + 255 `<script type="application/ld+json">` blocks per page.
#    The `'unsafe-inline'` on the static layer is the documented bridge until the
#    Pages Function middleware ships nonces via HTMLRewriter (see functions/_middleware.js).
#
# 2. Functions middleware (`functions/_middleware.js`) overrides this CSP for HTML
#    responses with the architecture's exact production policy (nonce + strict-dynamic +
#    Turnstile/Cal allowlist). `_routes.json` ensures the middleware runs on every HTML
#    response and is skipped for `/_astro/*` immutable hashed assets.
#
# Security header suite (architecture AAR §14 lines 615-618):
#   X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#   X-Frame-Options: DENY
#   Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
#   Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
#   Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload (PROD only)
#
# v9.2 deltas vs v6.10.34:
#   + script-src: https://challenges.cloudflare.com (Turnstile), blob: (SW pre-cache)
#   + frame-src: https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://cal.com https://*.cal.com
#   + worker-src: 'self' blob: (service worker)
#   + object-src: 'none'
#   + upgrade-insecure-requests
#   + report-uri: /api/csp-report (deferred — architecture doesn't define endpoint)
#   - Removed the implicit blanket 'unsafe-inline' on connect-src (now explicit)
#   + HSTS preload (production only; max-age=0 on preview/localhost to avoid bind failure)
#
# v9.2 STRIDE/security audit gates (architecture AAR §13 + §14):
#   - XSS via inline script: nonce middleware closes the static-layer gap
#   - Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options DENY + frame-ancestors 'none'
#   - MIME sniffing: nosniff
#   - Referrer leak: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
#   - Feature abuse: Permissions-Policy denies camera/mic/geo
#   - MITM: HSTS (prod) + upgrade-insecure-requests
#   - CDN compromise: object-src 'none' denies plugin execution

# Default for all routes — full security header suite + CSP.
# The `/*` glob is Cloudflare's "all routes" pattern.
# Per the architecture AAR §14, every middleware exit path (200/204/404/413/429/500)
# passes through `withSecurityHeaders()`; `_headers` is the static fallback.
# Production CSP includes Turnstile + Cal.com + worker-src for SW; the inline allowance
# is the bridge until middleware ships nonces (see functions/_middleware.js).
# report-uri is forward-looking — the endpoint is deferred to Phase 3c per architecture.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' trade-off (binding):
#   - script-src 'unsafe-inline' = bridge until middleware (architecture AAR §14 lines 635-644)
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline' = bridge until middleware OR per-style hash (architecture AAR §14)
#   - 'unsafe-eval' = REFUSED per security_engineer standing orders + architecture AAR §14
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://challenges.cloudflare.com blob:; script-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://cal.com https://*.cal.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests; report-uri /api/csp-report

# Immutable hashed assets — strict CSP (no 'unsafe-inline' needed).
# These are Astro-emitted JS/CSS bundles with no inline content. Cloudflare's
# Pages default cache-control was max-age=0 + must-revalidate, costing ~50-100ms
# TTFB on every repeat visit; the immutable directive makes them cache for 1 year.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Page HTML — short cache, must revalidate so deploys propagate fast.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Sitemap + feeds — also short so crawlers see updates.
/sitemap*.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/feed*.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
  Content-Type: application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8

# LLM-friendly markdown alternates — moderate cache.
/llms*.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Service worker — must not be cached aggressively or the browser will refuse updates.
# `service-worker-allowed` lets the SW control the scope above its path.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /

# Proof videos — long cache + explicit range support. v6.11.18 fix:
# Cloudflare Pages default `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# was stripping Accept-Ranges for the /proof/*.mp4 files, breaking
# video scrubbing in Chrome. Explicit immutable cache + range header
# ensures Chrome can seek the video without redownloading the whole file.
/proof/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Accept-Ranges: bytes
